sections.text:
- drawn between the looks before and after the moment, not extrapolated from the past;
- widened to cover where the face was for 0.1 s either way (`face_blur_pad_seconds`), which absorbs the decoder's and
  OBS's frame timing;
- a missed look or two bridged (up to `face_blur_bridge_seconds`, 1 s) when the same face is found again;
- held 0.3 s after a face was last seen and put up 0.3 s before it is first seen (it was probably there, turned away),
  covering both where it was and as far again as it was moving between its first (or last) two sightings, so that a
  face walking in from the edge is covered back to the edge, not only where it was first found;
- each box averaged with its neighbours in time (the detector's boxes wobble by a few percent);
- a margin added, and the rectangle snapped out to whole blocks.

More faces than patches per camera (8, `face_blur_slots`) are covered by joining the nearest together, never by
leaving one out. A patch moving with a face moves its OBS item rather than hiding one and showing another.
